`vq->split.vring.desc` is the shared vring descriptor table — coherent DMA memory that the device (or a malicious host in a guest's view / an attackers' device) can write concurrently. The kernel's own bookkeeping of the chain length is in `vq->split.desc_extra[].next`, which mirrors the device table's `next` field at add time. The `while` condition reads `vq->split.vring.desc[i].flags` directly from the shared table on every iteration (the "validated/authoritative" copy would be `desc_extra[i].flags`, which IS maintained in kernel memory and is used for `~VRING_DESC_F_NEXT` clearing at line 621-623 when use_dma_api).

